<section id="follow">
<h2>One PR read crosses both processes.</h2>
<ol>
<li>The gateway receives a chat sender identifier and builds a canonical subject. It asks the model for a response using that agent’s configured tools.</li>
<li>The model can use a script to read a PR and filter its structured result. The interpreter is not Bash and cannot spawn the host’s <code>gh</code> executable.</li>
<li>The broker checks the peer and subject mapping, evaluates static rules, then invokes the provider inside its configured HTTP limits. The result returns to the script and model.</li>
</ol>
<p>Rules do not judge intent: an allowed action can still be harmful. <a href="/guides/access/#policy">The PR-commenter decision</a> shows how separate grants and constraints fit together; <a href="/guides/runtime/#workflow">the shell example</a> shows what the model can compose.</p>
